WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:02.180
Somewhere, someone is writing

2
00:00:02.180 --> 00:00:04.240
you a very polite lie.

3
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:06.580
Here are five myths about it,

4
00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.530
answered.

5
00:00:08.118 --> 00:00:09.118
Myth one.

6
00:00:09.118 --> 00:00:11.668
Phishing only comes by email.

7
00:00:12.298 --> 00:00:13.138
The fact:

8
00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:15.658
it also comes by text message,

9
00:00:15.658 --> 00:00:18.158
phone call, and QR code.

10
00:00:18.158 --> 00:00:20.788
Different doors, same trick.

11
00:00:21.353 --> 00:00:22.413
Myth two.

12
00:00:22.413 --> 00:00:24.966
My bank may ask for my OTP,

13
00:00:24.966 --> 00:00:26.743
to verify me.

14
00:00:27.622 --> 00:00:28.342
The fact:

15
00:00:28.342 --> 00:00:31.062
never share an OTP, PIN or CVV

16
00:00:31.062 --> 00:00:31.475
with anyone.

17
00:00:31.475 --> 00:00:34.182
Banks and government bodies do

18
00:00:34.182 --> 00:00:36.762
not ask for sensitive details by

19
00:00:36.762 --> 00:00:37.562
text.

20
00:00:38.284 --> 00:00:39.584
Myth three.

21
00:00:39.584 --> 00:00:42.184
If it is urgent, it must be

22
00:00:42.184 --> 00:00:44.824
real. Who would hurry you for no

23
00:00:44.824 --> 00:00:45.714
reason?

24
00:00:46.307 --> 00:00:47.207
The fact:

25
00:00:47.207 --> 00:00:49.207
urgency is the bait.

26
00:00:49.207 --> 00:00:50.707
Pause and verify.

27
00:00:50.707 --> 00:00:53.047
If a caller creates panic, hang

28
00:00:53.047 --> 00:00:53.847
up.

29
00:00:54.155 --> 00:00:55.175
Myth four.

30
00:00:55.175 --> 00:00:57.775
A QR code is always safe to

31
00:00:57.775 --> 00:00:58.575
scan.

32
00:00:59.340 --> 00:01:00.160
The fact:

33
00:01:00.160 --> 00:01:02.560
check the web address first.

34
00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:04.880
Never scan a stranger's code,

35
00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.260
and look for a sticker pasted

36
00:01:07.260 --> 00:01:08.770
over a real one.

37
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:10.497
Myth five.

38
00:01:10.497 --> 00:01:13.927
If I was fooled, it is too late.

39
00:01:14.394 --> 00:01:15.074
The fact:

40
00:01:15.074 --> 00:01:16.654
act at once.

41
00:01:16.654 --> 00:01:19.874
Call 1930, report on the

42
00:01:19.874 --> 00:01:22.334
cybercrime portal, and tell your

43
00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.134
bank.

44
00:01:24.475 --> 00:01:25.555
For GS3:

45
00:01:25.555 --> 00:01:29.035
email, text, call, QR.

46
00:01:29.035 --> 00:01:30.895
Never share an OTP.

47
00:01:30.895 --> 00:01:33.035
Verify the urgent.

48
00:01:33.035 --> 00:01:34.828
Report on 1930.

49
00:01:35.401 --> 00:01:37.621
A pause before every click.

50
00:01:37.621 --> 00:01:39.591
Small, and strong.
